hadiths[53]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7517","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Qurashi told us, in Kufa, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Zaid bin told us Al-Hubab, Zayd bin Uqba Al-Hadrami told us, Khair bin Nu’aym told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: {And the dawn and ten nights} [Al-Fajr: 1] “The tenth part of the sacrifice and the odd-numbered prayer on the Day of Arafat and the intercession on the Day of Sacrifice” This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7517 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7518","Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih in Baghdad and Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us that it had passed, saying: Abu Qalaba al-Raqqashi told us, Yahya bin Kathir ibn Dirham, Shu’bah told us, Ahmad ibn Ja’far told us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad told us Ibn Bakr, told us by Shu’bah, on the authority of Malik Ibn Anas, who said: I heard Amr Ibn Muslim, saying: I heard Sa’id Ibn Al-Musayyab, saying: Umm Al-Musayyab said: Salamah, may God be pleased with her: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever sees the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah and wants to sacrifice, let him not take “His nails or hair until he sacrifices.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7518 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7519","Abdan bin Yazid Al-Daqqaq told us, about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, who said: “When the tenth of Dhul-Hijjah begins, do not take from Your hair or your nails until your sacrifice is slaughtered.” This is authentic evidence for the hadith of Malik, even if it is authentic.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7519 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7520","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Anazi told me, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Yazid bin Abdul Rabbo told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us He said: I asked Muhammad bin Ajlan about taking hair during the ten days, and he said: Nafi’ told me that Ibn Umar passed by a woman taking Her son felt sad about the ten days and said: “If you had delayed it until the Day of Sacrifice, it would have been better.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7520 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7521","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Othman Al-Adami told us, Muhammad bin Mahan told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Qatada narrated that he said: A man from Al-Atiq came and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab narrated that Yahya bin Omar said: “Whoever buys a sacrifice on the tenth, let him He takes some of his hair and nails.” Saeed said: Yes, so I said: About whom, Abu Muhammad? He said: On the authority of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7521 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7522","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya told us, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Qart, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The greatest of days in the sight of God is the Day of Sacrifice, then the Day of Qur.” Five or six camel animals were presented to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they began to add Which of them should he start with, and when it came to its south - he said a light word that I did not understand, so I asked the one next to him and he said - he said: “Whoever wants, he can cut it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7522 - True"
"7523","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad bin Habib al-Hafiz told us, Abu Salamah Yahya bin Al-Mugheerah Al-Madani, Abdullah bin Nafi’ told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Sulayman bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not bring anything near to God Almighty on the Day of Sacrifice that is more beloved to Him.” God Almighty from the shedding of blood, and that it will come on the Day of Resurrection with its horns, hairs, and hooves, and that the blood will fall from God Almighty. “In a place before it falls on the earth, so they may enjoy it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7523 - Suleiman Wah"
"7524","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Al-Nadr bin Ismail told us Al-Bajli, Abu Hamza Al-Thumali told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said: “O Fatima, go to your sacrifice and witness it, for every sin you have committed will be forgiven at the first drop of its blood, and say: “Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my life, and my death belong to God, Lord of the worlds, with no partner, and with that I was commanded, and I am one of the Muslims.” Imran said: I said: O Messenger. By God, this is for you and for your family in particular. Is that for you, or for Muslims in general? He said: “No, but for Muslims in general.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “And it was witnessed by the hadith of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7524 - Indeed, Abu Hamza is very weak"
"7525","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Dawud bin Abdul Hamid told us, Amr bin Qais Al-Malali, on the authority of Atiya, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Fatima May the peace and blessings of God be upon her: “Go to your sacrifice and witness it, for with the first drop of its blood that drips, your previous sins will be forgiven.” She said: O Messenger of God, is this for us, the Ahl al-Bayt in particular, or for us and the Muslims in general? He said: “Rather, for us and for Muslims in general.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7525 - Atiyah Wah"
"7526","Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Abu al-Walid Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Ahmad bin Burd al-Antaki told us, told us Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hunaini, Hisham bin Saad told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: Gabriel, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, descended to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “O Gabriel, how did you see Our feast? He said: The people of heaven bragged about him. Know, O Muhammad, that a lamb from a sheep is better than a lamb from goats, and that a lamb from a sheep is better than a lamb from cows, and that a lamb from a sheep is better than a lamb from cows. A sheep is better than a sheep, a sheep is better than a camel, and if God had known a better slaughter, he would have sacrificed it for Abraham, peace and blessings be upon him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration.” And they did not bring it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7526 - Isaac Hulk"
"7527","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Ayoub bin Suwayd told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, on the authority of Yazid Ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Al-Baraa Ibn Aazib, may God be pleased with him, that a man said to him: We hate deficiency in the horns and ears, so he said to him Al-Baraa: hate for yourself whatever you want and do not forbid it to people. Al-Baraa said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Four things are not sufficient for sacrifice: one-eyed woman whose fault is clear, and one whose part is broken.” “Her pillars are clearly broken, and the sick is clearly sick, and the lean one that cannot be cleaned.”"
"7528","Abu Al-Abbas Uqba told us, Al-Rabi’ told us, Ayyub bin Suwayd told us, Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, similar to this. Al-Rabi’ said in his book With two chains of narration, he said: Al-Awza’i narrated the hadith of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, with a valid chain of narration. They did not narrate it, rather Muslim narrated it. May God Almighty have mercy on him. The hadith of Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ubaid bin Fayrouz, on the authority of Al-Baraa, and it is about what was reported from Muslim, may God have mercy on him. Because the transmitters disagreed about it, and the most authentic of it is the hadith of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7527 - Ayoub bin Suwayd was deemed weak by Ahmad"
"7529","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, and Saeed bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ayyash bin Abbas, narrated to them on the authority of Issa bin Hilal Al-Sadfi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them, said that a man came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “I was ordered to bring Al-Adha is a holiday that God has made for this nation.” The man said: “If I find nothing but a female lamb, or my family’s sheep, or their lamb, I will slaughter it.” He said: “No, but trim your nails, trim your mustache, and shave your pubic hair. That is the completion of your sacrifice in the sight of God Almighty.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7529 - This is an authentic hadith"
"7530","Abdullah bin Ishaq bin Al-Khurasani Al-Adl told us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Malaab bin Hayyan told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Shu'bah and Sa'id reported on the authority of Qatada, who said: I heard Jarari ibn Kulayb, a man from among them, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade sacrificing limbs of the horn and ear. Qatada said: I mentioned that to Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab. He said: “The limb Half or more.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7530 - True"
"7531","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Shurayh Ibn Al-Numan, on the authority of Ali Ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade sacrificing one another or facing one another.” “Or fair-haired, or clumsy, or stumpy.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7531 - True"
"7532","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Shuraih ibn al-Nu’man, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded us to look towards the spring.” And the ear should not be sacrificed with a muqabla, a muqabla, a shrouqa, or a clumsy one.” Abu Ishaq said: “The muqabla means the tip of its ear being cut off, and the muqabla: What was cut off from the side of the ear, and the “sharqa”: the one that was slit, and the “cracked”: the one that was pierced. “This is an authentic hadith, all of its chains of narrations, but they did not narrate it.” I think it is due to an addition mentioned by Qais bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, stating that they did not use Qais as evidence. Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi narrated to us. Ahmad bin Ubayd Allah Al-Zaki told us, Abu Kamil Muzaffar bin Mudarrak told us, Qais bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Shuraih, on the authority of Ali Radi On his authority, so he mentioned something like it. Qais said: I said to Abu Ishaq: Did I hear it from Shurayh? He said: Ibn Ash’wa told me, on his authority."
"7533","Abu Bakr bin Attab told us, Yahya bin Jafar bin told us. . . . ., Wahb bin Jurayj reported, told us by my father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Hajiya bin Adiy, that a man asked Ali, and he was satisfied May God narrate it, on the authority of Al-Baqarah? He said: About seven. He said: Kastorah al-Qarn? He said: It will not harm you. He said: The lame? He said: When you reach the ritual, he said: “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to look out with the eye and the ear.” Narrated by Sufyan. Al-Thawri and Shu’bah, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Hajiya bin Adi"
"7534","As for the hadith of Sufyan, he said: A man asked Ali about the cow. He said: About seven, and he said: The horn is broken? He said: No problem. He said: The lame? He said: When you reach the ritual, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to look out with the eye and the ear.”"
"7535","So Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, and Abu Omar Al-Hawdi told us, they said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail, he said: I heard Hajjayyah bin Adiy, saying: I heard Ali, and a man asked him about the cow, and he said: About Seven, he said: And he asked him about Maksoorah Al-Qarn? He said: It will not harm you. He said: And he asked him about lameness? He said: When the ritual has been performed, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to look out with the eye and the ear.” These are all of the chain of narrations. Authentic, and they did not use as evidence the evidence of Ibn Adi, who was one of the major companions of the Commander of the Faithful Ali, may God be pleased with him.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7535 - True"
"7536","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Bahr Al-Bari told us, my father told me, Issa bin Yunus told us, Thawr ibn Yazid told me, Abu Humaid al-Ru’ayni told me, Yazid ibn Khalid al-Masri told me, he said: I came to Utba ibn Abd al-Sulami, and I said: O Abu Al-Walid, I went out to seek the victims, but I did not find anything I liked except Thurmaa, so I hated her. What do you say? He said: Why did you not bring it to me and I said: Glory be to God, it is permissible for you and it is not permissible for me? He said: Yes, you doubt, but I do not doubt. Rather, “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the hairless, the hairless, the skinny, and the obese.” “And the broken” and the yellowing woman whose ear is removed until her earmuffs are exposed, and the uprooted woman whose horn was removed, and the skinny woman who is thinned. The same, and the Shiites who do not follow the sheep out of weakness and weakness, and the broken ones, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7536 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7537","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Ali bin Asim told us, Ibn Tawus told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is not permissible for a single, weak, or barren person to make a vow.” “And the worded woman is all her doctors.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7537 - Ali bin Asim is weak"
"7538","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al Ansari told us, I am Abdullah bin Abi Shaybah, Abdullah told us Ibn Idris, Asim Ibn Kulayb narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: We were commanded in the battles by the Companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we were in Persia, so they failed. On the Day of Sacrifice, we must take the musanah, and we used to take the musanah by the two or three stems. Then a man from Muzainah stood up among us and said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The trunk is repaid from what the second one is repaid from.” It was narrated by Al-Thawri, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, and the companion named him Mujasha’ bin Masoud Al-Sulami."
"7539","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, He said: We were with Mujashi bin Masoud Al-Sulami in a battle, and the casualties were great, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The trunk will pay off.” From what the second will be repaid.” It was narrated by Shu’bah, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, and he did not name the companion."
"7540","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man from Muzainah or Juhaynah, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were A day or two after the sacrifice, they were given two trunks and took a second, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The trunk suffices for what it suffices.” “From it is the second one.” This is a hadith about which there is disagreement on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, and it is something that the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, did not narrate, and I have stipulated for myself It is used as evidence, and the hadith in my view is authentic after they unanimously agreed on mentioning the companion about it, then the imam of the industry named it Sufyan bin Saeed Al-Thawri. May God be pleased with him.”"
"7541","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Abd told me Al-Rahman bin Salman bin Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Qusayt, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Because It is more beloved to me to sacrifice a leg of a sheep than to sacrifice a female goat.” Narrated by Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Qurashi, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abd. Allah bin Qusayt, and he named the companion Umm Salamah."
"7542","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Masdad told us, Abdul-Ala told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Because I sacrifice a leg of sheep.” Is more beloved to me than sacrificing a female goat.” This hadith was transmitted on the authority of Abu Hurairah."
"7543","Sheikh Abu Bakr told us, Ubaid bin Sharik Al-Bazzar told us, Abu Al-Jamahir Muhammad bin Othman Al-Tanukhi told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi, on the authority of Abu Thifal, on the authority of Rabah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “The blood of a white man is more beloved to me than the blood of two black men.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7543 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7544","Abu Bakr bin Ubaidah told us, Ali bin Zaid Al-Faraidi told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hunaini told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Thifal, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A young lamb is better than a young lamb.” The goat
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7544 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7545","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Qaza’ah bin Suwayd told us, Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Salama bin Junada, on the authority of Hanash bin Al-Harith, Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, narrated to me that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. With a lean, vile leg of sheep and a lean, fat leg of a goat. He said: O Messenger of God, he is the better of the two. Should I sacrifice him? He said: “Sacrifice it, for God is All-Sufficient.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7545 - Qaza bin Suwayd is weak"
"7546","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Muhammad bin Jahdam told us, Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Abi Habiba Al-Ashhali, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, “that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent Saad bin Abi Waqqas with a herd of sheep, and he divided them among his companions, and a male goat remained of them, which he sacrificed in the “His Umrah” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7546 - Ibrahim is different in his justice"
"7547","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha and Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with them, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, sacrificed two big, fat, salty rams, with two horns and two wavy horns. He slaughtered one of them and said: “O God, on behalf of Muhammad and his nation.” Who bears witness to you of monotheism and bears witness to me of conveying the Message?
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7547 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7548","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani and Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told me, saying: Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, My father told me, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sacrificed a ram.” “A horned camel that walks in darkness, eats in darkness, and looks in darkness.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7548 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7549","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he said: Al-Darawardi told me, on the authority of Rabih Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abi Sa`id al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, slaughtered a ram. He approached the place of prayer and then said: “O God, this is on my behalf and on behalf of those of my nation who did not sacrifice.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7549 - True"
"7550","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Nadr informed us, Muawiyah bin Amr told us, Zaydah told us, about Statement by Al-Bajli, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Abu Sariha, who said: “My family made me behave unfairly after I learned the Sunnah. We used to sacrifice a sheep and two sheep for The People of the House. My family said: Our neighbors claim that we are stingy. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7550 - True"
"7551","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Hatim ibn Abi Nasr, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Nasi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The best sacrifice is the horned ram, and the best of the shroud is the cloak.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7551 - True"
"7552","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told me, Ibrahim bin Yusuf Al-Razi told us, Hisham bin Ammar told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Saeed bin Abd told us. Al-Aziz, on the authority of Yunus bin Maysarah bin Halbas, on the authority of his father, he said: I went out with Saad Al-Zarqi, and he was with him, to buy the victims, so he indicated To a ram whose head was bruised, not as high as the rams, and he said: “As if it were the ram that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sacrificed.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7552 - True"
"7553","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Yahya told me Bin Abdullah bin Salem, and Ya’qub bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Amr, the client of Al-Muttalib, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah, and on the authority of a man, from Bani Salamah told us that Jabir bin Abdullah told them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for the people on the Day of Sacrifice. When he finished During his sermon and prayer, he sacrificed a ram and slaughtered it himself, and said: “In the name of God, and God is great. O God, this is on my behalf and on behalf of those who did not.” He will sacrifice from my nation.”"
"7554","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bakr Al-Adl told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, he informed us Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, Ibn Abi Rafi’ told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered He handed over his sacrifice and then said: “O God, this is on my behalf and on behalf of my nation.”"
"7555","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told us, Abu Aqeel Zahra bin Ma’bad told me, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Hisham, and he had met the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his mother had taken him. Zainab bint Humaid went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he was young, so he wiped his head and prayed for him. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He sacrifices one sheep on behalf of all his family.” These hadiths are all authentic with chain of narrations regarding the permissibility of sacrificing a sheep. One on behalf of a group whose number is incalculable, contrary to those who imagine that it is only sufficient for one person. News has been narrated in “The sacrifice on behalf of the dead.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7555 - True"
"7556","Among them is what Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us. Bishr bin Musa Al-Asadi and Ali bin Abdul Aziz Al-Baghawi reported, saying: Muhammad bin Saeed bin Al-Asbahani told us, Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasna, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Hanash, who said: Ali sacrificed, may God be pleased with him. With two rams, a ram on behalf of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a ram on his behalf, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me to sacrifice on his behalf.” So I will sacrifice forever.” “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and this Abu Al-Hasana is: Al-Hasan bin Al-Hakam Al-Nakha’i.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7556 - True"
"7557","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Yazid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, Abu told me Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered I sacrificed it while traveling, then he said: “O Thawban, prepare its flesh.” So I continued to feed him from it until we came to Medina. “This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7557 - True"
"7558","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, they said: Abd told us Al-Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: On the day of Al-Hudaybiyyah, we slaughtered seventy camels, each for a camel. Ten, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let the cows share in the sacrificial animal.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. Al-Badanah was narrated on the authority of Ashra, also on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7558 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7559","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Ibrahim bin Hilal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and the sacrifice came and we shared the cow. On the authority of seven, and in Al-Jazur on the authority of ten. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7559 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"7560","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi told us, in Baghdad, Abu Al-Ahwas Muhammad bin Al-Haytham Al-Qadi told us, Abu Salih Abdullah bin Salih, Al-Layth bin Saad narrated to me, on the authority of Ishaq bin Buzraj, on the authority of Zayd bin Al-Hasan bin Ali, on the authority of his father, May God be pleased with them. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us during the two Eids to wear the best clothes we can find, and to perfume ourselves with the best things.” We find, and we sacrifice the fattest ones we find, a cow for seven and camels for ten, and we declare the takbeer and be calm. And dignity: “If it were not for the ignorance of Ishaq bin Buzraj, I would have judged the hadith to be authentic.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7560 - Had it not been for Ishaq’s ignorance, I would have ruled that he was healthy"
"7561","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Utbah Ahmad bin Al-Faraj told us, Baqiyya bin Al-Walid told us, Uthman bin Zufar told us Al-Juhani, Abu Al-Aswad Al-Sulami told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: I was on the seventh day with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. On his journey, we reached the sacrifice of sacrifice, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to collect a dirham. Each of us collected a dirham, so we bought a sacrifice for seven dirhams. And we said: O Messenger of God, we have been oppressed by it. He said: “The best of sacrifices are the most precious and the fattest.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us. And he greeted, and he took it, man for man, and man for man, and man for hand, and man for hand, and man for horn, and man for horn, and he slaughtered the seventh, and they said takbir upon it. Everyone
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7561 - Othman bin Zufar is trustworthy"
"7562","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail Ibn Ulayya told us, Ziyad told us Ibn Mikhraq, on the authority of Muawiyah Ibn Qurra, on the authority of his father, that a man said: O Messenger of God, I am more merciful to a sheep than to slaughter it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you have mercy on her, God will have mercy on you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7562 - True"
"7563","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya the martyr, may God have mercy on him, told us, Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak told us Al-Aishi, Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that a man had sex with a sheep wanting To slaughter her while sharpening his blade. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do you want to kill her to death? Would you please sharpen your blade before you “Lay her down.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7563 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"7564","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simmak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: {And indeed the devils inspire to their guardians} [Al-An’am: 121] He said: “They say, ‘What was slaughtered?’” So he mentioned the name of May God bless it, so do not eat it, and as long as the name of God is not mentioned over it, eat it.” Then God Almighty said: “And do not eat of that over which the name of God has not been mentioned” [Al-An’am: 121] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7564 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7565","Al-Hasan bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Abdullah bin Ayyash told us, Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever has money and does not offer a sacrifice, then he They approach our place of prayer.” And he once said: “Whoever finds plenty of food and does not slaughter, let him not approach our place of prayer.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7565 - True"
"7566","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Abdullah told me Ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, narrated to him on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Whoever finds plenty of food and does not sacrifice with us, let him not sacrifice it with us.” “They bring our place of prayer near.” Abdullah bin Wahb stopped it, but more than one trustworthy person is acceptable, and Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri is more than trustworthy."
"7567","Professor Abu Al-Walid and Abu Bakr bin Abdullah told me, saying: Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told us. Al-Muqaddami, Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, my father told me, Utbah bin Abdul-Malik Al-Sahmi told us, that Zurarah bin Karim bin Al-Harith bin Amr, narrated to him that Al-Harith bin Amr, narrated to him on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever wishes, may branch, and whoever wishes, may not branch, and whoever He may prostrate himself if he wishes, and whoever wishes may not prostrate himself, and in the case of sheep as their sacrifice.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7567 - True"
"7568","Abu Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahboubi informed us, Sa`id ibn Masoud informed us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sa`id ibn Iyas informed us Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O people of Medina, “Do not eat the meat of the sacrificial animals for more than three days.” They complained about this to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that they had dependents, family members, and servants, and he said: “Eat, be fed, and keep yourselves safe.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7568 - True"
"7569","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Zuhayr bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Sharik bin Abdullah bin Abi Nimr, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father and his uncle, Qatada bin Al-Numan, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “Eat the sacrifices and save.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not narrated by “the last book of sacrifices.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7569 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
